lines=['# D4.1 text errata — NSSCAS Mathematics 8227','','24 November 2026. Owner Vitalis; PLANNER Codex. NIED December 2020 syllabus. D4 repairs are independently confirmed; **D4.1 diff-only review and Vitalis exact-manifest approval remain pending. Stage D only.**','','## What changed, and what did not','','The two remaining authority residues now distinguish the binding OD-6 principle from proposed MR03-OPS-D4 per-datum mechanics. The shared operations add exactly these three clarifications, identically in the source policy, MR03, all nine work-order lines and all 27 policies plus merged/register copies:','','> An A/B is on a datum when it lies in the datum\'s first-use part or a later part whose working uses the misread data, whether or not that criterion\'s own value changes.','','> Eligibility is judged at first use for the connected question.','','> Eligible follow-through never overrides MR09 (no F.T. into a supplied result) or OD-1 answer-only rules.','','The operational rules remain proposed, not an additional owner decision. No ledger algorithm, fixture tag, gross/net score, deduction slot, tariff, criterion type, domain, parameter, canonical answer, Bloom label or recipe/classification version changed. Counts remain **9 recipes /14 choices /42 cases /27 parts /83 branch marks**, Bloom13 Apply /1 Analyse, decks19/20/17, facets38+1 conditional-only and99 demands outside direct pilot scope. Version remains0.1.4; classification remains8227-pilot-design-0.1.1.','','## Listed errata and notes','','| ID | Before → after | Evidence |','|---|---|---|','| D4-S01 | Two body sentences attributing the per-datum unit to OD-6 → explicit OD-6 principle / proposed MR03-OPS-D4 mechanics | vector WO73; implicit exemplar125; exact spans below |','| D4-S02 | Undefined datum scope and overly broad override → the three exact clauses quoted above; identical propagation | source policy, subject MR03,9WOs,27parts and generated copies |','| D4-N01 | Absolute render_path → repository-relative path to the identical render/hash | visual-d4-independent-checks.py; two relocated rebuilds |','| motion-D4-06 | Accidental “D1 D4 changed-scope confirmation” → historical “D1 short check confirmed” | PLAN11 |','| shared/visual-D4-04 | Undated decision6 → “16 November owner decision 6 (visual demands)” | capability-gaps and recipe-contract |','| shared-D4-03 / trig-D4-03 | Named stale round/gate/status/receipt labels → current D4/D4.1 labels and D4 receipts | source fields/generators and regenerated records |','| motion-D4-01 | Bare2/6 outcome → printed-interval R1 decision, T-independent R2 primitive and attempted-primitive/both-bounds R5 rationale | motion WO75 |','| motion-D4-02 | Unqualified best single/pair156/168 → best visible156/168; derived(d/a,T)162/168 also disclosed | motion WO73 |','| motion-D4-03 | Version included in exposure key → provenance only; no exposure reset. Old versions named0.1.1–0.1.3 | motion WO25/35 |','| motion-D4-05 / calc-D4-04 | Copied mixed/proof branch notes → branch-appropriate polynomial, exponential and standalone-gradient notes | policy propagation script and source/merged/register copies |','| calc-D4-01 | Unqualified C4→5 9/9 → explicitly product route; divided/log-absolute/explicit-root cases remain E/F fixtures | implicit WO148/exemplar151; no new score ruling |','| visual-D4-02 | Incomplete register anchor → 2023 P2 Q6 AWARD05 citation plus WO95 proposed B2www clause | visual deviation input and regenerated21-row checkpoint |','| visual-D4-03 / shared-D4-07 | Record-keeping caveats now disclosed | paragraphs below; no mathematical change |','','Visual policies retain common operational fields and some generic visual eligibility tails; criterion-specific details remain in the work orders. The old D4 report’s claim of uniformly part-specific tails was too broad. This errata does not invent new part-specific marking rules.','','The trapezium strict-unseen summary **3→2 was already corrected in D4**. It was a stale summary correction to match generated-fresh capacity2, with mathematical packing3 separately named. D4.1 leaves the archived D4 value2 unchanged and makes no domain/capacity change.','','The product-route C misread can still score9/9 under the existing canonical treatment of an ineligible datum. Other proof routes, datum identity, competing misreads for one mark, ambiguous visual notation and previously named E/F cases remain carried. This text pass does not settle them or claim runtime marker acceptance.','','## Verification','','The no-score guard passes: 3 canonical designs,2 derived design/register records,18 fixture/domain files,42 distinct canonical examples and70 fixed gross/net ledger records (overlapping records, not70 unique submissions). It rejects5 seeded semantic changes. Only named text/status/path/hash leaves may differ; numeric values, types, array order, tags, score records, versions and mathematical data remain exact. See `planning/d4-1/no-score-change-check.json` and its documented allowlist.','','The normal author rebuild passes twice: **18 commands per round,28 byte-identical derived outputs,25 subprocess negative fixtures rejected**, plus5 inline motion-domain and4 inline ledger rejections. Prior independent D4 audits remain historical reviewed evidence, rather than being silently re-labelled current acceptance.']
